About Nebius: 
Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.
Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.
Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;D.
 The role 
 Nebius is looking for a Sales Strategy and Operations Manager (IC) to&nbsp; partner directly with our sales leadership team to shape and execute Nebius’ go-to-market strategy and drive operational excellence across the full revenue lifecycle for our selling teams in the Americas market . 
 You will act as a strategic business partner to Sales leadership and support the execution of the go-to-market strategy through data-driven insights, process optimization, and operational excellence. &nbsp; 
 This role will own key processes related to quarterly planning cycles, territory alignment, forecast accuracy, pipeline health, and CRM governance. You will ensure operational consistency across the region and provide visibility into performance metrics that drive revenue outcomes. &nbsp; 
 We are looking for a proactive and detail-oriented professional who combines strong analytical skills with structured thinking and execution rigor. The ideal candidate is comfortable working with large datasets, building dashboards, improving sales processes, and collaborating cross-functionally with Finance, Marketing, and GTM stakeholders. &nbsp; 
 You thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth environment, can manage multiple priorities simultaneously, and communicate effectively with stakeholders at different levels of the organization. &nbsp; &nbsp; 
 You’re welcome to work remotely in the United States. 
 Your responsibilities will include: &nbsp; 
 Support Sales leadership in weekly forecast reviews and pipeline inspections &nbsp; 
 Maintain and improve forecast tracking models and reporting structures &nbsp; 
 Build and maintain dashboards in CRM / BI tools to monitor bookings, pipeline generation, conversion rates, and attainment &nbsp; 
 Ensure CRM data hygiene and enforce standardized pipeline management practices &nbsp; 
 Support territory alignment updates and account ownership changes &nbsp; 
 Assist in quarterly planning cycles (target tracking, headcount tracking, performance visibility) &nbsp; 
 Partner with Finance on revenue visibility and reporting alignment &nbsp; 
 Monitor lead routing logic and GTM workflows across HubSpot and Salesforce &nbsp; 
 Identify process gaps and propose operational improvements &nbsp; 
 Support documentation of GTM processes and internal playbooks &nbsp; 
 Assist with system enhancements and new tool rollouts &nbsp; 
 Provide ad-hoc analysis to support business decisions &nbsp; 
 We expect you to have: &nbsp; 
 6-7+ years of experience in Sales Operations, Revenue Operations, Business Operations, or a similar analytical function (preferably in Cloud, SaaS, or other technology) &nbsp; 
 Strong hands-on experience with CRM systems (Salesforce and HubSpot) &nbsp; 
 Experience working with forecasting processes and pipeline reporting &nbsp; 
 Proficiency in Excel/Google Sheets and SQL; experience working with large datasets &nbsp; 
 Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple priorities &nbsp; 
 Clear communication skills and ability to collaborate cross-functionally &nbsp; 
 Comfortable working in a fast-paced, scaling environment &nbsp; 
 Key employee benefits in the US: 
 Health insurance: &nbsp;100% company-paid medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and families.
 401(k) plan:&nbsp; Up to 4% company match with immediate vesting.
 Parental leave: &nbsp;20 weeks paid for primary caregivers, 12 weeks for secondary caregivers.
 Remote work reimbursement: &nbsp;Up to $85/month for mobile and internet.
 Disability &amp; life insurance : Company-paid short-term, long-term and life insurance coverage.
 Pay Transparency 
We offer competitive compensation and benefits packages. Actual compensation will be determined based on job-related factors, including experience, skills, qualifications, the level at which the candidate is hired, and geographic location, consistent with applicable law.
Base Compensation Range
 $137,600 &mdash; $172,000 USD 
 Benefits &amp; Perks: 
Competitive compensation
Career growth and learning opportunities
Flexibility and ownership
Collaborative and innovative culture
Opportunity to work on impactful AI projects
International environment and talented teams
 What's it like to work at Nebius: 
Fast moving&nbsp;- Bold thinking&nbsp;- Constant growth&nbsp;- Meaningful impact&nbsp;- Trust and real ownership&nbsp;- Opportunity to shape the future of AI&nbsp;
 Equal Opportunity Statement: 
Nebius is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and diverse workplace and to providing equal employment opportunities in all aspects of employment. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.
Applicants must be authorized to work in the country in which they apply and will be required to provide proof of employment eligibility as a condition of hire.&nbsp;
If you need accommodations during the application process, please let us know.

Do you like making it easier for a Sales team to do its best work? Do you enjoy owning the details that keep deals moving, while also spotting where the process could work better? And do you get satisfaction from turning repetitive work into a simpler, smarter way of working? 
 AIHR is looking for a Senior Sales Operations Manager to join our Revenue Operations team. You’ll help support more than €10 million in annual deal value , working closely with Sales leadership while owning the operational processes that move deals from opportunity to collected revenue. 
 About AIHR 
 Founded in 2016 with the mission to future-proof HR, the Academy to Innovate HR (AIHR) has become the world’s market leader in online training for human resources (HR) professionals. We have a global customer base spread across 140+ countries, amongst which companies like Unilever, Reckitt, Goldman Sachs, Philips, Deloitte, Nike, Heineken, and UBS. It is our goal to continuously upskill and empower 1,000,000 HR Professionals. 
 We are an international team of 90+ people, driven by excellence, innovation, and a hunger to grow in everything we do. As such, we strive to provide the world’s best courses and excellent support to our customers while continuously optimizing every aspect of our work. With over 30 nationalities, our team is diverse, yet we all share a few traits: we're friendly, enthusiastic, and great team players. 
 Being a fast-growing company, working at AIHR means taking on a lot of responsibility and getting countless opportunities to develop yourself in new areas and potential to craft your own role. 
 Role and Responsibilities 
 As our Senior Sales Operations Manager, your job is to make it easier for Sales to do great work. This is a hands-on role with a broad view of the commercial journey. You’ll work on how Sales operates, support leadership with better insight, and own processes such as the Deal Desk, vendor registration, invoicing, collections, and order-to-cash. 
 We see those responsibilities as connected. Being close to the day-to-day work gives you the context to see where time is being lost, where a process no longer works, and where the same problem keeps coming back. We want someone who is comfortable doing the work themselves, but who does not simply accept unnecessary manual work because “that’s how we do it.” 
 This role is a combination of keeping things moving today and making sure they work better tomorrow. 
 Your responsibilities include: 
 Improving how Sales works. You use data, feedback, and your understanding of the day-to-day work to identify where things can be better. That could mean redesigning a workflow, improving reporting, clarifying ownership, creating a better operating rhythm, or removing manual steps that no longer add value. 
 Helping Sales leadership improve performance. You look beyond individual requests and help spot patterns across the Sales organization. Where are deals slowing down? What does the data tell us about why? Are we missing information in HubSpot that would help Sales, Marketing, or leadership make better decisions? You turn those observations into practical recommendations and are comfortable challenging existing ways of working when the data points somewhere else. 
 Owning and improving the Deal Desk. When a deal needs something outside the standard process, you help move it forward. This can include approvals, documentation, commercial questions, vendor or supplier registration, procurement portals, questionnaires, and coordination across internal and external stakeholders. You take care of the immediate need, while also looking for patterns that could make the next request simpler. 
 Owning order-to-cash and collections. You take responsibility for turning booked revenue into collected cash. Collections is a meaningful and hands-on part of the role: monitoring outstanding invoices, following up with customers, picking up the phone when that is the best way to resolve an issue, and working with Sales, Finance, procurement teams, and other stakeholders to clear payment blockers. You also look at the process behind the work — reducing overdue balances, improving follow-up, and finding ways to make order-to-cash more effective over time. 
 Working AI-first. You actively use AI and automation where they can make the work more efficient or improve the quality of the outcome. That might mean analyzing patterns in Sales data, speeding up vendor registration, improving a recurring workflow, or removing repetitive administrative work. As part of RevOps, you are expected to try new approaches, keep what works, and share useful ways of working with the wider team. 
 Connecting the dots across teams. Many commercial processes cross Sales, Finance, Customer Experience, Marketing, Operations, and other parts of the business. You help create clarity around ownership, bring the right people together, and make sure decisions turn into action. 
 You’ll work with tools including HubSpot, Gong, Atlassian, QuotaPath, Zapier, Google Workspace , and a growing set of AI tools and internal AI workflows. We do not expect you to arrive as an expert in every system. We do expect you to be comfortable learning how they fit together and questioning whether we are using them in the best way. 
 Success in this role is not simply an empty queue or a dashboard that looks good. It is reliable day-to-day execution combined with steady improvement in how Sales operates. 
 On a typical day 
 On Monday morning, you start by getting a view of the commercial week ahead. You check active deals in HubSpot, outstanding operational requests, the payments inbox, and anything else that needs attention. 
 During the RevOps stand-up with the RevOps team, you talk through priorities. An Account Executive is working on an enterprise opportunity where the customer's procurement team needs AIHR registered as a vendor. Several invoices need follow-up. You have also noticed a group of deals spending longer than expected in one stage of the pipeline. 
 The vendor registration comes first. You use one of our existing AI workflows to help complete the documentation, gather any missing information internally, and get the process moving. While doing that, you notice that part of the information the workflow relies on is out of date. Rather than working around it, you fix the source and make sure the next registration is easier. 
 Later, you turn to the stalled opportunities. You dig into the data, speak with the Sales team, and find that Account Executives are not consistently recording meeting outcomes. That makes it difficult to understand why certain MQLs progress while others do not. 
 The answer may not be “Sales needs to update HubSpot more.” You look at why the information is not being captured in the first place and whether the workflow can be made easier for reps while still giving Marketing and leadership the information they need. You believe it’s easier to change a process than to change human behaviors. 
 After lunch with colleagues in the office, you spend time on collections. Some invoices need a straightforward reminder. Others need more persistence. You follow up with customers, get on the phone where needed, and work through issues involving purchase orders, invoicing details, procurement processes, or internal ownership. 
 This work is part of the role, not something sitting outside it. And because you are doing it yourself, you see first-hand which issues are one-offs and which ones point to something we should fix. 
 On another day, you sit down with Sales leadership to look at commercial performance. You are not there simply to report what happened. You help interpret what is behind the numbers and what we might do differently. 
 You also regularly connect with Neal, Head of CX & Operations , and colleagues across Business Operations. Some weeks you will spend more time on live operational work; other weeks give you more room to improve reporting, build an automation in Zapier, clean up a process in HubSpot, or work on a broader RevOps project. 
 That balance is part of the role. 
 By Friday, a good week means the work got done: customers were followed up, deals moved forward, Sales had the support they needed, and something in the way we operate is now a little clearer or easier than it was before. 
 We offer 
 A high-impact role working closely with Sales leadership and the wider Business Operations organization; 
 The opportunity to own important commercial processes while also improving how our Sales organization works; 
 Managing a growing deal volume of €10M+ per year across the commercial funnel; 
 Competitive, benchmarked compensation; 
 The opportunity to shape your own day-to-day work; 
 Regular growth talks and support to reach your career goals; 
 Flexible working hours & working from home arrangements; 
 A high degree of autonomy in a vibrant, result-driven, inclusive, and international team; 
 Access to AI tools including the latest AI models so you can automate repetitive work and improve how you operate day to day; 
 A beautiful office right across Rotterdam Central Station (Milleniumtower) and a satellite office in Amsterdam; 
 26 paid holidays per year + 1 extra day for the first 5 years you work at AIHR 
 Exchange any 2 public holiday days for 2 other days of your choice; 
 Work from anywhere policy, where you can work abroad for 20 days in a calendar year; 
 Pension plan; 
 4 Trust days per year (ad-hoc recovery days to take whenever you're overwhelmed, exhausted, or need to deal with something personal); 
 Access to OpenUp mental health platform; 
 Personal development budget, training, and we pay for the books you read; 
 All public transport expenses covered (NS Business Card); 
 MacBook + all other equipment you need to do your work; 
 Daily lunch prepared by a chef, regular drinks, and fun team activities; 
 Free access to the office gym. 
 Get a taste of the AIHR experience and check out our AIHR Benefits Guide ! 
 Apply for the job 
 Are you excited to become our Senior Sales Operations (SalesOps) Manager? Then we'd love to hear from you! We are looking to hire for this role as soon as we find an eligible candidate. 
 P.S. Research shows that while men apply to jobs when they meet an average of 60% of the criteria, women tend to apply only when they meet 100% of them. So if you think you have what it takes, but don't necessarily meet every single point above, please still apply. We'd love to consider you and see if you could be a great fit. 
 Who you are 
 We are looking for someone who combines strong operational execution with commercial awareness. 
 You are comfortable getting into the details and doing repetitive work when it needs to be done. At the same time, you tend to notice when the same issue keeps appearing and start thinking about how to remove it rather than simply processing it faster. 
 You are likely a strong fit if you: 
 Have solid experience in Sales Operations, Revenue Operations, Commercial Operations, or an end-to-end order-to-cash role within a B2B environment, including hands-on exposure to collections; 
 Understand how B2B Sales processes work and can use data, operational signals, and feedback from Sales to identify where things could improve; 
 Are comfortable owning processes such as the Deal Desk, vendor registration, invoicing, collections, and order-to-cash , even if you have not owned every one of them previously; 
 Are confident working with CRM data, spreadsheets, reporting, and operational tools. Experience with platforms such as HubSpot, Gong, Atlassian, QuotaPath, Zapier, or Google Workspace is useful, but curiosity and the ability to learn matter more than knowing our exact stack; 
 Communicate clearly across Sales, Finance, Operations, Marketing, and leadership, and are comfortable raising a different point of view when you believe there is a better way forward. 
 You do not need to match every point perfectly. What matters most is that you can combine ownership, attention to detail, analytical thinking, and the judgment to know when to execute the process and when to change it.

Are you passionate about transforming the way people and organizations learn and develop? Imagine partnering with the world's most prestigious brands, guiding them through transformative learning journeys that redefine industry standards. At AIHR, we are on a quest to find a full-time Customer Success Manager (with Ed-tech experience) who will exceed our clients' expectations, turning every learning initiative into a remarkable story of performance enhancement and organization-wide impact. Embark on this thrilling adventure with us and play a pivotal role in shaping the future of the HR industry! 
 About AIHR 
 Founded in 2016 with the mission to future-proof HR, the Academy to Innovate HR (AIHR) has become the world’s market leader in online training for human resources (HR) professionals. We have a global customer base spread across 140+ countries, amongst which companies like Unilever, Reckitt, Goldman Sachs, Philips, Deloitte, Nike, Heineken, and UBS. It is our goal to continuously upskill and empower 1,000,000 HR Professionals. 
 We are an international team of 100+ people, driven by excellence, innovation, and a hunger to grow in everything we do. As such, we strive to provide the world’s best courses and excellent support to our customers while continuously optimizing every aspect of our work. With over 30 nationalities, our team is diverse, yet we all share a few traits: we're friendly, enthusiastic, and great team players. 
 Being a fast-growing company, working at AIHR means taking on a lot of responsibility and getting countless opportunities to develop yourself in new areas and potential to craft your own role. 
 Role and Responsibilities 
 As a Customer Success Manager (with Ed-tech experience) , you are responsible for enabling your B2B clients to run successful learning initiatives and create a culture of learning. At AIHR, we call this role in AIHR as a Learning Consultant rather than a Customer Success Manager because your focus goes beyond account management - you act as a strategic advisor, guiding customers in designing and implementing impactful learning journeys. 
 You manage the entire relationship: from onboarding to learning adoption, up until the renewal. Once a customer signs, you are introduced to the various important stakeholders (e.g. CHRO, Head of L&D, HR Managers). You create a plan with your client to ensure they achieve their learning and business goals. Throughout the journey, you stay in contact with your clients to advise, consult, enable, and inspire further learning and adoption of our platform. You support Growth Account Executives with the renewal and expansion of your accounts. 
 You’ll have a mixed portfolio of mid-market and enterprise customers. Some clients will require an in-depth plan and continuous communication; others will just need advice on some best practices. You are successful when your client’s learners have shown improved work performance, not just when they complete a training program, and when the impact of AIHR leads them to want to continue our partnership. Ultimately, your client’s success is your success, and your goal is to develop their learners into T-shaped HR professionals. 
 On a typical day 
 You arrive at our beautiful office in Rotterdam or Amsterdam, grab a coffee, and after a brief chat with colleagues, you fire up your MacBook to check your calendar. You start by reviewing your portfolio in HubSpot, our single source of truth, paying close attention to the Customer Health Score to prioritize your actions for the day. 
 Your morning includes a Quarterly Strategic Check-in with a key client, where you present a compelling story of their progress using learning and engagement data you've analyzed with the help of a custom GPT. Afterward, you have a 1-1 with your manager, Emilie , to strategize on a renewal risk within your portfolio. Later, you spend time with Dieter, one of our superstar SMEs, to plan a thought leadership session with customer HumanX. 
 After a delicious lunch in the office with the team, you dedicate time to a new client, Canadian Nuclear Laboratories, documenting their business objectives to create their Joint Impact Plan. You then join a meeting with Jessica, our Growth Account Executive, to align on the commercial strategy for an upcoming renewal, ensuring you are working as a unified team. 
 Before the day ends, you contribute to an internal project, sharing customer feedback about new features and improvements with the product team, including feedback you summarized by feeding call transcripts into Gemini. 
 To wrap up the week, you join the team for a drink during our weekly activity, celebrating joint successes and getting to know new colleagues. 
 Who you are 
 Helping clients roll out learning initiatives successfully is nothing new for you. You’ve done this before, and you know you can do more than that. You want to be a strategic advisor and trustworthy consultant to your client, as you know that if they experience impact with AIHR’s platform, they will see massive skill development, performance improvements, and a learning culture change. 
 Furthermore, you have: 
 4+ years of experience in a client-facing role, such as a (Learning) Consultant, L&D Professional, or Customer Success Manager, specifically within the Ed-Tech or E-learning industry; 
 A proven track record of managing a portfolio of 50+ clients and skillfully prioritize to maximize impact across your portfolio; 
 Demonstrable experience successfully building and maintaining relationships with multiple stakeholders; 
 Strong English proficiency with the ability to discuss proposals, write clear copy, and push back on or challenge customers constructively; 
 A natural ability to ask insightful follow-up questions to diagnose core challenges and co-create solutions with clients; 
 Experience in the ed-tech industry, supporting clients in implementing and scaling learning initiatives; 
 The ability to think commercially, identify growth opportunities, and discuss how HR initiatives impact overall business performance; 
 Strong skills in using data from tools like HubSpot and Excel to derive insights and present a clear story of progress and value to customers; 
 Experience using generative AI tools (e.g., ChatGPT) for tasks like content creation and workflow automation is essential; 
 To set you up for success in this role, we are specifically looking for candidates with external-facing customer experience (not in-house L&D roles) and a background in education, e-learning, or ed-tech. While we believe many skills can be learned on the job, these experiences are essential, as they provide the foundation needed to drive impact in our environment. 
 We offer 
 A key role in shaping the education of tens of thousands of Human Resource professionals from all over the world through our courses; 
 Competitive, benchmarked compensation; 
 The opportunity to shape your own day-to-day work; 
 Regular growth talks and support to reach your career goals; 
 Flexible working hours & working from home arrangements after your onboarding; 
 A high degree of autonomy in a vibrant, result-driven, inclusive, and international team; 
 A key role in a fast-growing scale-up company; 
 A beautiful office right across Rotterdam Central Station (Milleniumtower) and a brand new office in Amsterdam; 
 26 paid holidays per year + 1 extra day for every year you work here + you can exchange any 2 public holiday days for 2 other days of your choice; 
 Pension plan; 
 5 Mental health days per year; 
 Access to OpenUp mental health platform; 
 Personal development budget, training, and we pay for the books you read; 
